<%- include('partials/header') %>
<main id="main-content">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">About Amicus</li></ol></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">About Amicus Shipping LLC</p>
      <h1>Maritime experience behind the tools.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Amicus grew from work around vessels, cargo and port calls. Today that experience shapes connectivity and coordination tools for the people moving between ship and shore.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="founder-heading" id="jivko-atanassov">
    <div class="container split founder-profile">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The person behind Amicus</p>
        <h2 id="founder-heading">Jivko Atanassov</h2>
        <figure class="founder-portrait">
          <img src="<%= site.founder.image %>" width="680" height="808" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Jivko Atanassov, founder of Amicus Shipping LLC">
          <figcaption>Founder, Amicus Shipping LLC</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="lead">Ship agency, vessel operations and cargo inspection came before the digital tools.</p>
        <p>Jivko's maritime background includes ship-agent work, a marine superintendent role and petroleum inspection. His work has involved vessel arrivals and departures, terminal coordination, crew and spares arrangements, and cargo quantity checks.</p>
        <p>At Amicus, his marine consulting work has included cargo and bunker surveys. That background brings a concrete view of shipping: schedules change, several parties need the same information, and small gaps in communication can affect the next movement.</p>
        <p>His professional record also includes building spreadsheet templates to simplify document processing. Applying technology to a repeated operational task is a thread that continues through Amicus today.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-soft" aria-labelledby="about-progression-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">From port work to digital services</p><h2 id="about-progression-heading">The work shapes what we build.</h2></div><p>One maritime perspective connects three parts of the business.</p></div>
      <div class="grid-three">
        <article class="feature-card"><p class="eyebrow">Understand the operation</p><h3>People, timing and handovers.</h3><p>Agency and vessel operations require coordination between crew, terminals, service providers and the ship. Information needs to reach the person who can act on it.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><p class="eyebrow">Prepare the journey</p><h3>Connectivity before departure.</h3><p>A joining crew member needs travel details, maps and a way to contact the coordinator. The Amicus eSIM store provides a place to arrange mobile data for covered travel destinations.</p><a class="text-link" href="/seafarers">Solutions for seafarers</a></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><p class="eyebrow">Connect the participants</p><h3>A shared crew-change workflow.</h3><p>Amicus Crew Change brings trip information, journey stages and messages together for participating crew and coordinators.</p><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.crewLandingUrl %>">Explore Amicus Crew Change</a></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="credentials-heading">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Professional background</p><h2 id="credentials-heading">Experience you can put in context.</h2></div>
      <div class="stack"><p>Jivko's professional record lists IFIA certification during his past petroleum-inspection roles. That work included cargo gauging, temperature measurement and quantity calculations. These references describe his professional history, rather than a current company accreditation.</p><p>We keep the same care in describing the products. Travel eSIMs depend on terrestrial mobile networks. Crew-change arrangements still need local confirmation. Inspection question practice does not award a qualification.</p><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.inspectionLandingUrl %>">About the inspection study tool</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-dark"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">A direct conversation</p><h2>Tell us about your next crew rotation.</h2><p>Share the travel countries, crew numbers and the communication problem your team needs to solve.</p></div><div><a class="button button-light" href="<%= site.inquiryUrls.connectivity %>" data-event="operator_inquiry">Discuss Crew Connectivity</a></div></div></section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
